48: \nL49: Open today\nL50: \nL51: How you fit\nL52: \nL53: 92%\nL54: \nL55: Strong match on your objective\nL56: \nL57: From your contacts\nL58: You already know two people here.\nL59: \nL60: Elena worked with you in 2024.\nL61: \nL62: Pulled from your Career Vault\nL63: \nL64: The onboarding launch you shipped in 2026.\nL65: \nL66: Cut time-to-value 31% — added to your story for this role.\nL67: \nL68: WHAT'S INSIDE\nL69: ## Four parts. One memory.\nL70: \nL71: Tell Teal Pro something once and it turns up everywhere it's useful. The win you log today is the proof in next month's resume, the story in an interview, and the reason a role gets flagged as a fit.\nL72: \nL73: 01 · Career Vault\nL74: \nL75: ### You never start from a blank page\nL76: \nL77: One place that holds every project, win, and skill you've collected — so the thing you did two years ago is right there when it finally matters.\nL78: \nL79: 02 · Opportunity Fit\nL80: ### Stop spending nights on the wrong roles\nL81: \nL82: See how a job lines up against your experience and what you're after before you apply, instead of finding out three weeks later.\nL83: \nL84: 03 · Resume & Prep\nL85: \nL86: ### Walk in ready, not rushed\nL87: \nL88: Your resume, your outreach, and your answers — all built from what you've actually done, and tailored to the role in front of you.\nL89: \nL90: 04 · People & Follow-Ups\nL91: ### No one slips through the cracks\nL92: \nL93: The people connected to your search stay close, and you get a nudge before a follow-up goes cold.\nL94: \nL95: CAREER VAULT\nL96: \nL97: ## You've done more than fits on a resume.\nL98: \nL99: The work you're proudest of rarely survives the one-page cut. Teal Pro holds onto all of it — the projects, the numbers, the moment it clicked — so when you need proof of what you can do, it's already waiting for you.\nL100: \nL101: cite7†Start your Career Vault →†pro.tealhq.com L102: \nL103: You\nL104: \nL105: Add\nL106: ## Career Profile\nL107: \nL108: Your career history, facts, and the spine of your resume\nL109: \nL110: Launched a new onboarding system Cut time-to-value by 31%.\nL111: \nL112: 2026\nL113: \nL114: Led design on a new product Worked across four teams from zero to launch.\nL115: \nL116: 2025\nL117: \nL118: Built a team of four Hiring, coaching, and operations.\nL119: \nL120: 2024\nL121: \nL122: Teal pulls from this whenever you tailor a resume or get ready for a conversation.\nL123: \nL124: PEOPLE & FOLLOW-UPS\nL125: ## Someone you know can open this door.\nL126: \nL127: Almost every job moves faster through a person than a portal — and you already know more of those people than you'd guess. Teal Pro keeps them next to the jobs they're connected to, and gives you a nudge when it's time to reach out.\nL128: \nL129: cite5†See how connecting Google helps → L130: \nL131: Live graph\nL132: \nL133: Filter\nL134: ## People\nL135: \nL136: Contacts, network, referrals, and relationships\nL137: \nL138: ER\nL139: \nL140: Elena Ruiz Offered to introduce you to the design team.\nL141: \nL142: Works there\nL143: \nL144: MO\nL145: \nL146: Maya Okafor Interview Thursday, already on your calendar.\nL147: \nL148: Alum\nL149: \nL150: JL\nL151: \nL152: Jordan Lee You worked together in 2024.\nL153: \nL154: 2nd\nL155: \nL156: Contacts and calendar attendees build your people graph.\nL157: \nL158: ON YOUR PHONE\nL159: ## Your career doesn't only happen at a desk.\nL160: \nL161: Teal Pro has a native iPhone app with everything you have on the web. Log the win on your walk back. Check who you're about to meet from the lobby. Keep things moving from wherever you happen to be — Teal Pro keeps up with you.\nL162: \nL163: 9:41 ▮▮▮\nL164: \nL165: Today\nL166: ## Good morning,\nL167: Maya.\nL168: \nL169: Your next moves\nL170: \nL171: Get ready for Thursday Three projects worth talking about.\nL172: \nL173: Opp\nL174: \nL175: Reconnect with Elena Ruiz You last spoke six months ago.\nL176: \nL177: People\nL178: \nL179: Add the onboarding launch While the numbers are fresh.\nL180: \nL181: Profile\nL182: \nL183: Read today's Career Digest Curated roles and market read.\nL184: \nL185: Digest\nL186: \nL187: Home People Opps Chat\nL188: \nL189: See what to do today The same next moves you'd see on the web, in your pocket.\nL190: \nL191: 9:41 ▮▮▮\nL192: \nL193: Live graph\nL194: ## People\nL195: \nL196: Who you know, and how\nL197: \nL198: ER\nL199: \nL200: Elena Ruiz Offered an introduction.\nL201: \nL202: Works there\nL203: \nL204: MO\nL205: \nL206: Maya Okafor Interview Thursday.\nL207: \nL208: Alum\nL209: \nL210: JL\nL211: \nL212: Jordan Lee Worked together in 2024.\nL213: \nL214: 2nd\nL215: \nL216: PN\nL217: \nL218: Priya Nair Emailed you last spring.\nL219: \nL220: 2nd\nL221: \nL222: Home People Opps Chat\nL223: \nL224: Check who you're meeting Pull up how you know someone, and when you last spoke, right before you walk in.\nL225: \nL226: 9:41 ▮▮▮\nL227: \nL228: Add to profile\nL229: ## What happened?\nL230: \nL231: Ran the client workshop and got everyone aligned on the new direction.\nL232: \nL233: Win Leadership Project\nL234: \nL235: Save it\nL236: \nL237: Teal will bring this back when it's relevant.\nL238: \nL239: Home People Opps Chat\nL240: \nL241: Capture a win on the spot Add it while it's fresh instead of trying to remember it later.\nL242: \nL243: CONNECT GOOGLE\nL244: ## Let us handle the part everyone gives up on.\nL245: \nL246: Nobody keeps their network organized by hand — it's tedious and it never stays current. Connect your Google account and Teal Pro takes care of it for you, using your contacts and Calendar context to build and maintain your network. It stays off until you decide to turn it on.\nL247: \nL248: YOUR CONTACTS\nL249: ### See who you already know\nL250: \nL251: Teal Pro brings in your Google contacts — including people you've emailed but never saved — so remembering everyone stops being your job.\nL252: \nL253:   * Discover you already know someone where you're applying\nL254:   * Walk in with an introduction instead of applying cold\nL255:   * Keep your notes right next to the job they belong to\nL256: \nL257: YOUR CALENDAR\nL258: ### Never lose track of a conversation\nL259: \nL260: Teal Pro looks at who you've met with and when, so it can tell you who you've spoken to recently and catch the follow-up before it slips your mind.\nL261: \nL262:   * See who you've genuinely been in touch with lately\nL263:   * Get a nudge to follow up while it still counts\nL264:   * Keep every interview attached to the right job\nL265: \nL266: What Teal Pro can and can't do\nL267:   * Teal Pro can only read — it never changes or deletes your contacts or calendar\nL268:   * Connecting is up to you, and Teal Pro works fine without it\nL269:   * Teal Pro never emails or messages your contacts for you\nL270:   * You can revoke Teal Pro's access at any time through your Google Account. For help disconnecting, contact membersupport@tealhq.com.\nL271: \nL272: FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS\nL273: ## Teal Pro FAQs\nL274: \nL275: What is Teal Pro?\nL276: \nL277: Teal Pro is where your whole career lives in one place. It remembers what you've done, helps you find the jobs actually worth going after, gets you ready for them, and keeps you on top of the people and follow-ups along the way — so you're not holding all of it yourself.\nL278: \nL279: What does Teal Pro keep track of?\nL280: Your experience, projects, wins, skills, goals, the jobs you're interested in, the people connected to them, and what you've already decided. You choose what gets saved.\nL281: \nL282: Do I have to connect my Google account?\nL283: \nL284: Not at all. It stays off until you turn it on, and Teal Pro works fine without it. Connecting just saves you from typing in your contacts and schedule by hand.\nL285: \nL286: What does Teal Pro do with my contacts?\nL287: It reads them so it can tell you when you already know someone at a company you're interested in, and help you ask for an introduction. Teal Pro doesn't change or delete your contacts, and never emails them for you.\nL288: \nL289: Why does Teal Pro want people I never saved as contacts?\nL290: Google keeps a separate list of people you've emailed but never added to your contacts. Most of us have far more of these than saved contacts — old colleagues, people from past interviews, someone who introduced you to someone else. Teal Pro reads them so you don't lose track of people you actually know.\nL291: \nL292: What does Teal Pro do with my calendar?\nL293: It looks at who you've met with and when. That's how it knows who you've been in touch with recently, and when to remind you to follow up after an interview. Teal Pro doesn't create, change, or delete anything on your calendar.\nL294: \nL295: How do I disconnect Google?\nL296: \nL297: You can revoke Teal Pro's access at any time through your Google Account. For help disconnecting, contact membersupport@tealhq.com.\nL298: \nL299: How do I control my data?\nL300: You can see what Teal has, correct it, and remove it. Our Privacy Policy has the full detail on what we collect, how we use it, and how long we keep it.\nL301: \nL302: HOW WE HANDLE GOOGLE DATA\nL303: \nL304: Teal Pro's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs adheres to the cite9†Google API Services User Data Policy†developers.google.com , including the Limited Use requirements.\nL305: \nL306: START WHERE YOU ALREADY ARE\nL307: ## You've already done the hard part. Let's put it to work.\nL308: \nL309: cite7†Get Teal Pro†pro.tealhq.com L310: \nL311: Teal Pro is a product of Teal Labs, Inc.\nL312: \nL313: © 2026 Teal. All rights reserved.\nL314: \nL315: cite10†Privacy Policy cite11†Terms of Service --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCareerflow - Your Career Copilot | Powerful AI Job Search Tools (https://www.careerflow.ai/)\nciteturn13view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/h